.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>I realize that the introduct=
ion (i.e., everything up to this point) turned out to be much longer than I=
 expected. Nonetheless, I think that this lengthy introduction is perhaps n=
ecessary to put the following lessons into context.</p><p>After going throu=
gh a large number of recent papers on reasoning models last month, I have p=
ut together a summary of the most interesting ideas and insights in this se=
ction. (References like =E2=80=9C[1]=E2=80=9D point to the corresponding pa=
pers listed at the end of the article.)</p><h3 class=3D"header-anchor-post"=
><strong>1. Reinforcement learning further improves distilled models</stron=
g><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-a=
